## Merge Authority

### The PR creation gate — applies to ALL agent types

**Agents must NOT create a PR until the user explicitly approves it.**

After pushing a branch and passing the quality gate, agents must:
1. Update `docs/ACTIVE_BRANCHES.md` — set status to `pushed, awaiting local verify`
2. Tell the user the branch is ready and ask: **"Ready for me to open the PR?"**

The user verifies locally, then says yes (or words to that effect). Only then does the agent run `gh pr create`. The same gate applies before opening the dev → prod promotion PR.

**Phil's explicit trigger phrases** (treat any of these as a "yes, create the PR"):
- "create a PR", "open the PR", "go ahead with the PR", "ready for PR", "looks good, PR it", "ship it", "looks good"

### Once the PR is open — agents run the full lifecycle autonomously

After Phil approves PR creation, agents handle everything and only surface genuine blockers:

1. **Every PR must run the full Copilot feedback loop before merge — two exceptions: release PRs and the active Copilot pause (see "Release-PR exception" and "Copilot pause exception" in the Unified Checklist section below).** While `docs/PENDING_REMINDERS.md` → **Copilot pause protocol** is unchecked, **do not** request Copilot, wait for Copilot, or block merge on missing Copilot review — use the substitute checklist in that reminder instead. For all other periods, for feature / fix / chore / refactor PRs — regardless of tier — the full loop runs.
   If Copilot has not reviewed yet, the `copilot-review.yml` workflow auto-requests Copilot on PR open and on every `synchronize` (push) event to path-filtered tiers (see "Copilot Auto-Review Setup" below). For pushes that miss the workflow's path filter — or if the workflow's step failed — the agent re-requests manually using `gh pr edit <N> --add-reviewer "@copilot"` (GraphQL-backed, gh ≥ 2.88). **Never use** the dead REST endpoint `POST .../requested_reviewers -f reviewers[]=copilot`: it returns 200 OK but silently no-ops since 2026-04-17 (see `docs/COPILOT_LEARNINGS.md` 2026-04-17 entry). See "Copilot Auto-Review Setup" below for the exact commands and the narrow skip list (truly empty / whitespace-only / lone version-bump commits). After each re-request, verify `requested_reviewers` shows `["Copilot"]`, then wait for Copilot's new review, process any net-new comments, and loop until one of the following exit conditions is met:
   - Copilot's latest review produces **zero net-new unresolved comments**, OR
   - Every net-new comment on the latest review is either fixed and resolved, or skipped with documented reasoning using one of the valid skip patterns (see "Always document skip reasoning" below), OR
   - The **3-round cap** is reached (see "Round cap — 3 iterations" below).

   Tier only affects **how** the agent engages with each comment, not **whether** the loop runs:
   - **Security tier** (touches `lib/auth.ts`, `lib/permissions.ts`, `lib/dev-session.ts`, `proxy.ts`, `prisma/schema.prisma`, `.github/workflows/**`): implement or escalate every comment. Use the decision framework conservatively — default to "implement" unless the skip criterion is airtight.
   - **Medium-risk tier** (touches `app/api/**`, `lib/**`, `prisma/migrations/**`, `components/**`) and **standard PRs** (neither of the above): use the decision framework (implement real bugs, skip only with one of the valid documented reasons). Log every implemented comment to `COPILOT_LEARNINGS.md`.
2. Auto-merge when all safe-to-merge conditions pass
3. Verify the dev deploy, then tell Phil: "Merged and deployed to dev. Verify when ready — say the word and I'll open the prod PR."
4. Wait for Phil to verify in dev and approve before opening the prod PR
5. Open the prod PR, merge it, verify the production health endpoint
6. Tell Phil: "Deployed to prod. Health check: 200 OK."

### Dependabot PRs (author login contains `dependabot`)

Agents are authorized to **auto-merge Dependabot PRs** once all safe-to-merge conditions pass. Dependabot auto-merge is **not** enabled at the repo level, so these PRs will otherwise sit open indefinitely.

**During the session-start checklist:** scan for any open Dependabot PRs. If CI is green, threads are zero, and no security-sensitive files are touched, enable auto-merge immediately:
```bash
gh pr merge <PR_NUMBER> --repo cp-build-dev-ops/command-center-reboot --squash --auto
```

The `Auto-Merge Ready PRs` workflow handles Dependabot PRs through the same safety gates (CI green, no security-sensitive files, no merge conflicts). A new CI run may be triggered when auto-merge is enabled — this is expected under `strict: true` branch protection and resolves automatically.

**Race condition when merging Dependabot PRs and opening a feature branch in the same session:**
If you merge Dependabot PRs at session start (with `--auto`) and then create and push a feature branch in the same session, those Dependabot commits may land on `dev` while your feature CI is still running — leaving your branch `BEHIND` and blocking auto-merge. To prevent this: immediately after opening any feature PR in the same session as Dependabot merges, run:

```bash
gh pr update-branch <PR_NUMBER> --repo cp-build-dev-ops/command-center-reboot
```

Do this proactively before waiting for CI. It is harmless if the branch is already current.

### Contributor PRs (Hannah or any other team member)

**Phil personally reviews and merges all contributor PRs.** No agent may auto-merge a PR authored by a team member. Copilot reviews contributor PRs that touch security or medium-risk paths; agents may assist by addressing Copilot comments if asked — but the merge decision belongs to Phil.

When a contributor PR is ready (CI green), post a notification and inform Phil in chat:
```
👤 PR #N by @username is ready for your review — [one sentence summary]. Link: [url]
```

### Safe-to-Auto-Merge Conditions (all must be true)

| Condition | How to verify |
|-----------|--------------|
| User has approved PR creation | Said yes in chat for this specific PR |
| CI green | `gh pr view <n> --json statusCheckRollup` — all `SUCCESS` or `NEUTRAL` |
| Zero unresolved Copilot threads — **all PRs** | `required_conversation_resolution: true` is enabled repo-wide — unresolved threads block merge on every PR, not just security ones. Run the thread check below for every PR before enabling auto-merge. |
| No merge conflicts | `gh pr view <n> --json mergeable` — `MERGEABLE` |
| PR does NOT touch security-sensitive files | See list below |
| PR does NOT modify `prisma/schema.prisma` | Schema changes need Phil's review |

**Thread check — run before every auto-merge, regardless of PR tier:**

```bash
gh api graphql -f query='
{
  repository(owner: "cp-build-dev-ops", name: "command-center-reboot") {
    pullRequest(number: PR_NUMBER) {
      reviewThreads(first: 20) {
        nodes {
          id
          isResolved
          comments(first: 1) {
            nodes { body author { login } }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}' --jq '.data.repository.pullRequest.reviewThreads.nodes[] | select(.isResolved == false) | "UNRESOLVED [\(.id)]: \(.comments.nodes[0].author.login): \(.comments.nodes[0].body[:150])"'
```

If any unresolved threads are returned: address each one (fix in code or document the skip reason), then resolve:

```bash
gh api graphql -f query="mutation { resolveReviewThread(input: { threadId: \"THREAD_ID\" }) { thread { isResolved } } }"
```

Only proceed to auto-merge once this query returns no output.

### Security-Sensitive Files — Require Phil's Review (unless he explicitly approves)

If a PR modifies any of these, **do not auto-merge — notify Phil instead**:
- `lib/auth.ts`, `lib/permissions.ts`, `proxy.ts`
- `prisma/schema.prisma`
- Any file containing `PERMISSIONS`, `hasPermission`, or `auth()`
- `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` (production deployment config)
- Any file that handles secrets or environment variables at runtime

**Override:** If Phil explicitly says to merge/deploy (e.g. "go ahead and merge", "deploy it", "fully deploy to prod"), treat that as his sign-off on security-sensitive files for that specific PR.

### How to Auto-Merge (after user has approved PR creation)

**Before enabling auto-merge — always confirm the branch is current:**

```bash
gh pr view <PR_NUMBER> --repo cp-build-dev-ops/command-center-reboot \
  --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus \
  --jq '"mergeable:\(.mergeable) mergeStateStatus:\(.mergeStateStatus)"'
```

- If `mergeStateStatus: BEHIND` → run `gh pr update-branch` first, then **wait** and re-check until the state is no longer `BEHIND` before proceeding. Do NOT enable auto-merge on a BEHIND branch — the merge may fire while the branch is still out of date.

```bash
gh pr update-branch <PR_NUMBER> --repo cp-build-dev-ops/command-center-reboot
# Wait ~15-30s, then re-check mergeStateStatus before continuing
```

Once the branch is confirmed current (not BEHIND), enable auto-merge:

```bash
gh pr merge <PR_NUMBER> --repo cp-build-dev-ops/command-center-reboot --squash --auto
```

**Immediately after enabling auto-merge — re-check `mergeStateStatus`:**

```bash
gh pr view <PR_NUMBER> --repo cp-build-dev-ops/command-center-reboot \
  --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus \
  --jq '"mergeable:\(.mergeable) mergeStateStatus:\(.mergeStateStatus)"'
```

- `mergeStateStatus: CLEAN` → auto-merge will fire once CI passes. Proceed to poll for `state:MERGED`.
- `mergeStateStatus: BEHIND` → branch fell behind again (another PR merged in the window). Run `gh pr update-branch` again and wait before re-checking. Do not enable auto-merge again until CLEAN.
- `mergeStateStatus: BLOCKED` → CI is passing but something else is preventing merge. Work through this checklist in order:
  1. **Unresolved threads** (most common) — run the thread check query above. If any `isResolved: false` entries exist, address and resolve them. This is the leading cause of `BLOCKED` after CI goes green.
  2. **Required check still pending** — `gh pr view <n> --json statusCheckRollup` — look for any check with no `conclusion` (still running).
  3. **Branch is stale post-update** — a `gh pr update-branch` merge commit can trigger a new required CI run. Check if `lint-and-test` needs to re-run.
  4. **Required review missing** — `gh api repos/cp-build-dev-ops/command-center-reboot/branches/dev/protection --jq .required_pull_request_reviews.required_approving_review_count` — if non-zero, an approval is required.

**Do not assume auto-merge will fire just because CI is green.** CI green + `BEHIND` = silently blocked. CI green + unresolved threads = silently blocked.

**Always poll until `state:MERGED` is confirmed — not just until CI goes green:**

```bash
for i in $(seq 1 20); do
  STATE=$(gh pr view <PR_NUMBER> --repo cp-build-dev-ops/command-center-reboot \
    --json state,mergeCommit --jq '"state:\(.state) sha:\(.mergeCommit.oid // "pending")"')
  echo "[$(date +"%l:%M:%S %p" | sed 's/^ //')] $STATE"
  echo "$STATE" | grep -q "state:MERGED" && break
  sleep 15
done
```

Only transition to deploy polling after `state:MERGED` is confirmed. If the loop exits without MERGED, diagnose — never declare success based on CI green alone.

### When to Interrupt Phil

Only escalate when genuinely needed:
- CI fails and you cannot diagnose/fix it after 2 attempts
- Merge conflict you cannot resolve automatically
- PR touches a security-sensitive file AND Phil has not explicitly approved
- Architectural decision with two valid approaches and real trade-offs

For everything else: handle it and report when done.

