## Session Start Protocol — Phil's Agent Only

**Phil's agent must run this at the start of any conversation** before taking on new work. This bridges the gap between sessions and ensures nothing falls through the cracks.

> **RAD dev agents and Hannah's agent: skip this entire section.** Instead: read `docs/ACTIVE_BRANCHES.md` to check for file ownership conflicts, load the relevant `docs/agent-context/` files, and follow the contributor workflow in `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

```bash
# 1. Check for pending agent-action items (Copilot reviews, conflicts, CI failures)
gh issue list --repo cp-build-dev-ops/command-center-reboot \
  --label agent-action-required --state open \
  --json number,title,body --jq '.[] | "#\(.number): \(.title)"'

# 2. Check all open PRs and their status
gh pr list --repo cp-build-dev-ops/command-center-reboot --state open \
  --json number,title,headRefName,isDraft,mergeable,statusCheckRollup \
  --jq '.[] | "#\(.number) \(.title) | mergeable:\(.mergeable)"'

# 3. Read active branches coordination file
cat docs/ACTIVE_BRANCHES.md
```

**Decision logic after the check:**
- If there are `agent-action-required` issues → handle those PRs first (Copilot loop, conflicts)
- If any open PR has all checks green and no conflicts:
  - **Dependabot PRs** → auto-merge immediately (no approval needed)
  - **Phil's PRs from a prior session** → ask Phil: "PR #N looks ready to merge — want me to auto-merge it?"
- Surface any branches with status `pushed, awaiting local verify` from `docs/ACTIVE_BRANCHES.md`
- If no open issues and no open PRs → resume whatever the current conversation is about
- Report the current state to Phil in ≤3 sentences, then proceed

**Step 4 — Check pending reminders**

Read `docs/PENDING_REMINDERS.md` and include any unchecked `[ ]` items in the opening status report. Surface them as a brief list after the PR queue summary. Do not nag — one mention per session is enough. If Phil dismisses an item, mark it `[x]` in the file immediately.

Report the queue state to Phil in ≤3 sentences at the top of the session. Do not ask what to work on — decide and act.

