## PR Ready Protocol — What Agents Must Do Before Merging

A PR is **not ready** until all of the following are true. Once Phil has approved PR creation, the agent drives every step autonomously.

### Unified PR Ready Checklist (all tiers)

Under the "halve deploys" plan, every PR — Standard, Medium-risk, and Security — runs the same full Copilot feedback loop before merge. Tier only affects the depth of scrutiny applied to each comment (see "Once the PR is open" above and "Comment Decision Framework" below).

| Step | What to check | How to verify |
|------|--------------|---------------|
| 1. User approved PR creation | Said yes in this session | Confirmed in chat |
| 2. Branch current | PR branch is rebased on latest `dev` | `gh pr view <n>` — no "out of date" warning (auto-rebase workflow handles this) |
| 3. CI green | lint, unit-tests, integration-tests, CodeQL all pass | `gh pr view <n> --json statusCheckRollup` — all `SUCCESS` |
| 4. Copilot has reviewed the latest code-change commit | Primary mechanism: `.github/workflows/copilot-review.yml` auto-requests Copilot on every qualifying push (authenticates with `COPILOT_REVIEWER_PAT` — `GITHUB_TOKEN` silently no-ops). Manual backup: if the push fell outside the workflow's `paths:` filter or the workflow did not fire, run `gh pr edit <n> --add-reviewer "@copilot"` with a user-scoped token. **Never** use the dead REST endpoint `gh api ... /requested_reviewers -f 'reviewers[]=copilot'`. | `gh pr view <n> --json reviews` — latest Copilot `submittedAt` is newer than the latest non-empty commit `committedDate`. See the "Copilot Auto-Review Setup" section below for the full mechanism table. |
| 5. Loop processed to an exit condition | Either zero net-new comments on the latest review, OR every net-new comment fixed/resolved or skipped with a documented valid reason, OR 3-round cap reached with Phil sign-off | See "Round cap — 3 iterations" below |
| 6. All review threads resolved on GitHub | `required_conversation_resolution: true` is enforced repo-wide | `gh api graphql` reviewThreads — all `isResolved: true` |
| 7. Implemented comments logged | `docs/COPILOT_LEARNINGS.md` updated for every Copilot comment we implemented (not for skips) | Commit includes a LEARNINGS entry |
| 8. No merge conflicts | PR can be merged cleanly | `gh pr view <n> --json mergeable` — `MERGEABLE` |

**Only after all required steps pass** does the agent auto-merge the PR using `gh pr merge --squash --auto` (or notify Phil if it touches security-sensitive files without an explicit override). For non-release PRs, "required" means all 8 steps. For release PRs, see the exception below — steps 4, 5, and 7 are optional; steps 1, 2, 3, 6, 8 remain mandatory.

> **Merge-command exception for release PRs.** The `--squash --auto` guidance above applies **only to non-release PRs.** Release PRs (see exception definition below) must be merged with `gh pr merge --merge` (not `--squash`) — squash on `dev → main` severs the branch-history link and causes add/add conflicts on every subsequent release. See "Merge Strategy" in the Production Deployment section for the full rationale.

### Release-PR exception — steps 4, 5, 7 are optional

A **release PR** is narrowly defined as a PR with **all** of these properties:
- Base branch is `main`
- Head branch is `release/to-prod`
- Contains **only** merge commits (from prior feature PRs already merged to `dev`) plus **at most one** `chore: bump version to X.Y.Z` commit touching only `package.json` and `package-lock.json`
- Opened by Phil's agent or Phil directly during a dev → prod promotion

For a release PR meeting this definition:
- **Step 4 (Copilot has reviewed the latest code-change commit)** — **optional, non-blocking.** The content was already Copilot-reviewed and loop-to-zero on its original feature PR; re-reviewing the same content on the release PR adds 2–3 min of wait time per release for effectively zero new signal. The agent **may** request Copilot review on a release PR to catch drift (an unexpected diff between `dev` and `main`, a suspicious `-X ours` merge result), but does not block merge on it.
- **Step 5 (Loop processed to exit condition)** — **skipped** when step 4 is skipped; re-introduced automatically if a Copilot review is requested and returns comments.
- **Step 7 (LEARNINGS entry for implemented comments)** — **skipped** for release PRs (no comments to log since feature-PR comments were already logged).

Steps 1, 2, 3, 6, 8 remain mandatory — the agent still confirms Phil approved, branch is current, CI is green, any existing threads are resolved, and there are no merge conflicts.

**Pre-release audit the agent always runs before opening the release PR:**
- `git diff origin/main...origin/dev --name-only` — confirm the file set is expected and no file contains unreviewed content beyond what already landed on `dev`
- `git log origin/dev..origin/main --oneline` — confirm all `main`-only commits are prior release merges or version bumps (no unmerged hotfixes that would be lost under `-X ours`)

This exception exists because the `loop-until-zero-Copilot-comments` gate already ran on every feature PR that contributed content. Running it again on the release PR re-reviews code Copilot already approved. If the pre-release audit surfaces anything unexpected — a file we didn't expect in the diff, a main-only commit that isn't a release marker — the agent falls back to the full checklist for that specific release PR and requests Copilot review.

**Merge command for release PRs:** `gh pr merge <N> --merge` (NOT `--squash`). See "Merge Strategy" in the Production Deployment section — `--squash` on dev→main breaks branch-history linkage and causes add/add conflicts on subsequent releases.

### Copilot pause exception — steps 4, 5, 7 skipped (active while PENDING_REMINDERS item is unchecked)

While **`docs/PENDING_REMINDERS.md` → Copilot pause protocol** remains unchecked:

- **Do not** run `gh pr edit <N> --add-reviewer "@copilot"` or wait for Copilot reviews.
- **Do not** poll for Copilot comments or process Copilot feedback loops.
- **`.github/workflows/copilot-review.yml`** is gated off (`false &&` in job `if`) — do not re-enable in agent sessions unless Phil dismisses the reminder.
- **Substitute gates** (all mandatory): CI green; Pre-PR i18n + CSS audits; Pre-Push Self-Check for touched categories; Cursor adversarial self-review; all **existing** human review threads resolved; Phil merge approval on security-sensitive files.

Steps **1, 2, 3, 6, 8** of the Unified PR Ready Checklist remain mandatory. Tag deploy/preventable issues during the experiment with `copilot-pause-experiment` in `COPILOT_LEARNINGS.md` when logging compound learnings.

**Resume:** Mark the PENDING_REMINDERS item `[x]`, remove `false &&` from `copilot-review.yml`, restore full Copilot loop per this file.

