Instead of auto-merging, post this comment on the PR and tell Phil in chat:

```bash
gh pr comment <PR_NUMBER> --repo cp-build-dev-ops/command-center-reboot --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
⚠️ **This PR requires Phil's review before merging**

All checks pass and Copilot comments are resolved, but this PR touches security-sensitive files that require human sign-off:
- [list the specific files]

Everything else is ready. Awaiting your approval to merge.
EOF
)"
```

Chat message: `⚠️ PR #N is ready but touches [file] — needs your eyes before I merge. Link: [url]`

### When Agents May Skip Copilot Suggestions

Document your reasoning when skipping. Valid reasons to skip:
- Suggestion conflicts with a project-wide constraint (e.g. ESLint incompatibility, intentional architectural decision)
- Suggestion is already handled by existing automation or a different PR
- Suggestion is purely stylistic and ESLint already enforces the convention

Invalid reasons to skip: "it seems fine as-is", "not sure", "low priority".

