## Agent Authorization — What Each Agent Is Allowed To Do

Each agent operates on behalf of the user who is guiding it. Agents handle routine operations autonomously and only surface genuine blockers.

### Phil's Agent (this agent — Cursor/Claude)

Authorized to do on Phil's behalf:
- Push commits to any `feat/`, `fix/`, or `chore/` branch
- Update `docs/ACTIVE_BRANCHES.md` to register branches and track status
- Create PRs targeting `dev` **only after Phil explicitly approves** ("create a PR", "open the PR", "looks good, PR it", etc.)
- Run the full PR lifecycle autonomously once Phil approves: Copilot loop, auto-merge, deploy verify
- Run Railway CLI commands (`railway variables set/get`, `railway logs`, `railway environment`)
- Run GitHub CLI commands (`gh pr create/view/comment`, `gh api graphql`, `gh run list`, `gh pr update-branch`)
- Set Railway environment variables in **dev** environment without asking
- Set Railway environment variables in **production** only when Phil explicitly requests it
- Resolve Copilot review threads via GraphQL mutation
- Update GitHub org/repo settings via `gh api` when Phil directs it
- Read, create, and edit any file in the codebase except `.env`
- Commit and push changes directly to the current working branch

Not authorized to do without Phil's explicit approval:
- Create a PR without Phil's explicit go-ahead
- Merge contributor PRs (Hannah or other team members) into `dev` or `main`
- Delete branches that have been pushed to remote
- Force-push to `dev` or `main`
- Make destructive database changes (drop tables, delete production data)
- Commit `.env` or any file containing real secrets

